       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose. The usual ceiling for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, and the OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg/day total**, split into a different schedule\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you intended, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording the confirmation. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
